HighInBC wrote:
> just a few questions:
> 
> 1. What is a good AC for a monk who does not use body armour or a
> sheild?

	At what point in the game? I ascended my monk with AC -25, which
was pretty painful... I think I was fortunate that the first altar was
the right one, because I'm not sure I would've made the second. Whether
you're doing weaponless matters, too... the faster you can kill things,
the fewer chances they'll have to hit back, and so the less you need a
good AC.

> 2. What combination of armour is best, some sort of comprimise between
> AC and special abilities of armour.

	My monk ascended with a cloak of magic resistance, speed boots,
Hawaiian shirt, helm of brilliance, and leather gloves, all enchanted up
to +4/5, and an amulet of reflection.

	Gauntlets of dexterity would've been better, of course, but I
didn't find any and didn't consider them worth burning a wish on.
Gauntlets of power hamper spellcasting too much for my tastes.

	I don't wish for artifacts, much less other classes' Quest
Artifacts, so I needed the CoMR. Otherwise, I probably would've used a
robe (and I actually had my starting one, enchanted up and fireproofed,
in my bag just in case). The Eyes of the Overworld provide magic
resistance, but relying on them is risky after Rodney's been awakened.

> 3. How many times can I charge a magic marker? 

	Once.

 > Is it worth it to write
> a scroll of charging to charge a magic marker?

	If it hasn't been charged before, and you don't have scrolls of
charging already on hand, yes. Generally, the first thing I do with a
freshly acquired magic marker is write and bless a scroll of charging to
keep on hand for when it runs out.

> 4. I have a naked AC of 1, I have heard you can go lower, but the
> priest has stopped giving further protection. Is there another way to
> get perm protection?

	You can still buy more, down to -10 or so, in theory. The
chances of actually getting it rather than just being thanked for your
generosity get lower and lower as you go, though. I usually give the
priest whatever gold I've got on hand, in appropriately-sized
installments, and sometimes I get down to 0 or -1, and then don't bother
any further... though, for a monk, it might be worthwhile to keep trying
until you can't find any more gold. Praying at an altar is a more
effective means of gaining more at that point (though make sure you've
sacrificed down your prayer timeout, so you don't piss your god off and
lose all your gains).

